IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`
IMPORT `wica-schedules`
IMPORT `wica-liability`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — GOAL 3: HOW MUCH COMPENSATION?
--
-- Earnings (First Schedule para 6; Fifth Schedule Part 3 paras 6-7), the
-- incapacity (ss 4, 15, 34L), and the five heads: death, total incapacity,
-- partial incapacity (with the Fourth Schedule), temporary incapacity
-- (ss 17, 34N), medical treatment (ss 16, 34M) — for employees (ss 14-17,
-- First Schedule) and platform workers (ss 34K-34N, Fifth Schedule), and the
-- seafarer adjustments of s 67.
--
-- Source: ../source/WICA2019.txt lines 418-456, 682-788, 1831-1938,
-- 3294-3315, 3707-4001, 4260-4724. The three formulas printed as images are
-- transcribed in ../source/PROVENANCE.md.

§ `Goal 3 — the amount of compensation`

§§ `Earnings — AME for an employee (First Schedule para 6)`

-- para 6(1): continuously employed by the same employer "for more than one
-- whole calendar month immediately before the date of the accident" — AME is
-- A / P: A the actual earnings in the computation period, the whole calendar
-- months immediately before the accident "(up to a maximum of 12 such months
-- ...)", and P the number of those months.
-- para 6(2): employed "for one whole calendar month or less" — AME is
-- (D x W x 52) / 12: D the average earnings per working day, W the average
-- working days in a week.
-- para 6(3) and (6) (the Commissioner may disregard or adjust a month, or
-- estimate earnings without reliable evidence) are discretions: their result,
-- if used, is what the caller supplies as A, D or W.
@ref First Schedule para 6(1), (2)
GIVEN e IS AN `Employee earnings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employee's AME from` e MEANS
    IF   e's `continuously employed for more than one whole calendar month`
    THEN IF   `P` AT MOST 0
         THEN REFUSE "para 6(1): no whole calendar month in the computation period"
         ELSE e's `actual earnings in the computation period` DIVIDED BY `P`
    ELSE e's `average earnings per working day` TIMES e's `average working days per week` TIMES 52 DIVIDED BY 12
    WHERE
        `P` MEANS IF e's `whole calendar months continuously employed before the accident` GREATER THAN 12
                  THEN 12
                  ELSE e's `whole calendar months continuously employed before the accident`

§§ `Earnings — ADE and AME for a platform worker (Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 6)`

-- para 6(1)(c): relevant daily earnings R = E / P; P is the days at work
-- providing the service before the accident if fewer than 90, otherwise 90.
-- para 6(1)(b): ADE = R x (100% - F); F is 20% on foot, by public transport or
-- by unpowered bicycle; 35% by personal mobility device, power-assisted
-- bicycle or motorcycle; 60% by any other motor vehicle.
-- para 6(1)(a): AME = ADE x 30.
@ref Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 6(1)(b)
GIVEN m IS A `Mode of transport`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction F for` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `on foot, by public transport or by a bicycle that is not power assisted` THEN 20%   -- (A)
    WHEN `by personal mobility device, power-assisted bicycle or motorcycle`       THEN 35%   -- (B)
    WHEN `by motor vehicle other than a motorcycle`                                THEN 60%   -- (C)

@ref Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 6(1)
GIVEN e IS A `Platform earnings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform worker's ADE from` e MEANS
    IF   `P` AT MOST 0
    THEN REFUSE "para 6(1)(c): no days at work providing the service before the accident"
    ELSE e's `relevant earnings in the lookback period` DIVIDED BY `P` TIMES (100% MINUS `the deduction F for` (e's `mode`))
    WHERE
        `P` MEANS IF e's `days at work providing the service before the accident` LESS THAN 90
                  THEN e's `days at work providing the service before the accident`
                  ELSE 90

@ref Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 6(1)(a)
GIVEN e IS A `Platform earnings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform worker's AME from` e MEANS
    `the platform worker's ADE from` e TIMES 30

-- para 6(2): the lookback period is "(a) ... at least 90 days ... — the
-- period of 90 days immediately before the date of the accident; (b) [where
-- also] on hospitalisation leave or medical leave for 7 or more consecutive
-- days ... — 90 + B, where B is the number of days ... on [such] leave; (c)
-- [fewer than 90 days] — the number of days ... at work providing that
-- platform service."
@ref Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 6(2)
GIVEN e IS A `Platform earnings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lookback period in days for` e MEANS
    BRANCH IF e's `days at work providing the service before the accident` LESS THAN 90
              THEN e's `days at work providing the service before the accident`                   -- (c)
           IF e's `days of hospitalisation or medical leave in a run of 7 or more` AT LEAST 7
              THEN 90 PLUS e's `days of hospitalisation or medical leave in a run of 7 or more`       -- (b)
           OTHERWISE 90                                                                         -- (a)

§§ `The incapacity (ss 4, 15, 34L)`

-- s 4(5): with permanent or current incapacity, "(a) partial incapacity ...
-- if ... the aggregate percentage of the loss of earning capacity ... is less
-- than 100%; or (b) total incapacity if ... 100% or more." s 4(2)(b): an
-- injury in the Fourth Schedule is permanent incapacity.
@ref s 4(2), (5)
GIVEN percent IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Outcome
`the s 4(5) outcome for a loss of earning capacity of` percent MEANS
    IF   percent AT LEAST 100
    THEN `permanent or current total incapacity`
    ELSE `permanent or current partial incapacity` percent

-- s 15(1)(b), s 34L(1)(b): current incapacity is "assessed at the earliest
-- opportunity but not earlier than 6 months after the date of the accident".
-- s 15(2), s 34L(2) and s 4(4): never for the diseases in s 10(1) or 34G(1).
@ref s 15(1)(b), (2); s 34L(1)(b), (2); s 4(4)
GIVEN assessed    IS A DATE
      accident    IS A DATE
      `a disease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a current-incapacity assessment on` assessed `is allowed for an accident on` accident `, a disease:` `a disease` IF
        NOT `a disease`
    AND assessed AT LEAST `add months` accident 6

§§ `Death, total and partial incapacity (First Schedule paras 1-3; Fifth Schedule Part 3 paras 1-3)`

-- para 1(2)-(3): the death amount is held between $76,000 and $225,000 for an
-- accident before 1 November 2025, and between $91,000 and $269,000 on or
-- after it. para 2(b)-(c): C is held between $97,000 and $289,000, or between
-- $116,000 and $346,000. The Fifth Schedule repeats the same figures.
@ref First Schedule para 1(2)-(3); Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 1(2)-(3)
GIVEN accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the death floor for an accident on` accident MEANS
    IF accident LESS THAN YMD 2025 11 1 THEN 76000 ELSE 91000

GIVEN accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the death cap for an accident on` accident MEANS
    IF accident LESS THAN YMD 2025 11 1 THEN 225000 ELSE 269000

@ref First Schedule para 2(b)-(c); Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 2(b)-(c)
GIVEN accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the C floor for an accident on` accident MEANS
    IF accident LESS THAN YMD 2025 11 1 THEN 97000 ELSE 116000

GIVEN accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the C cap for an accident on` accident MEANS
    IF accident LESS THAN YMD 2025 11 1 THEN 289000 ELSE 346000

GIVEN x     IS A NUMBER
      floor IS A NUMBER
      cap   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`held between the floor and the cap` x floor cap MEANS
    BRANCH IF x LESS THAN floor    THEN floor
           IF x GREATER THAN cap   THEN cap
           OTHERWISE x

-- para 1(1): death — "the AME of the deceased ... [times] the appropriate
-- factor in the second column of Table A according to the age on the next
-- birthday ... at the time of the accident", then para 1(2)-(3).
@ref First Schedule para 1; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 1
GIVEN ame      IS A NUMBER
      born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the death compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for an accident on` accident
    THEN `held between the floor and the cap`
             (ame TIMES `the Table A factor for age` (`the age on the next birthday, if born on` born `, at an accident on` accident))
             (`the death floor for an accident on` accident)
             (`the death cap for an accident on` accident)
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this accident date"

-- para 2(a)-(c): C — AME times the Table B factor, held between the floor and
-- the cap.
@ref First Schedule para 2; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 2
GIVEN ame      IS A NUMBER
      born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`C for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for an accident on` accident
    THEN `held between the floor and the cap`
             (ame TIMES `the Table B factor for age` (`the age on the next birthday, if born on` born `, at an accident on` accident))
             (`the C floor for an accident on` accident)
             (`the C cap for an accident on` accident)
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this accident date"

-- para 2: total incapacity — "the formula C + 0.25C". The cap bites on C, so
-- the most payable is 1.25 times the cap.
@ref First Schedule para 2; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 2
GIVEN ame      IS A NUMBER
      born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total incapacity compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident MEANS
    1.25 TIMES `C for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident

-- para 3(1): partial incapacity — C times the percentage of loss of earning
-- capacity (the Fourth Schedule's, or as assessed "assuming that it is
-- permanent"). para 3(2): several injuries in one accident are aggregated,
-- "but not so as to exceed ... the amount ... payable in respect of permanent
-- total incapacity" (1.25C). s 4(5)(b): an aggregate of 100% or more is total
-- incapacity, paid under para 2 (found by the independent test pass).
@ref First Schedule para 3; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 3
GIVEN ame      IS A NUMBER
      born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
      percents IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the partial incapacity compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident `, losses in percent` percents MEANS
    BRANCH IF sum percents AT LEAST 100              THEN `the total amount`   -- s 4(5)(b): total incapacity, para 2
           IF `aggregate` GREATER THAN `the total amount` THEN `the total amount`   -- para 3(2)
           OTHERWISE `aggregate`
    WHERE
        `C`                MEANS `C for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident
        `aggregate`        MEANS sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD `C` TIMES p DIVIDED BY 100) percents)
        `the total amount` MEANS 1.25 TIMES `C`

-- Fourth Schedule Note 3: "Loss of remaining arm, leg or eye if one has
-- already been lost, is to be the difference between the compensation for the
-- total incapacity, and compensation already paid or that which would have
-- been paid for the previous loss of limb or eye."
@ref Fourth Schedule Note 3
GIVEN `total incapacity amount` IS A NUMBER
      `for the previous loss`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Note 3 compensation for losing the remaining member, total` `total incapacity amount` `, previous` `for the previous loss` MEANS
    IF   `total incapacity amount` GREATER THAN `for the previous loss`
    THEN `total incapacity amount` MINUS `for the previous loss`
    ELSE 0

-- One answer for the lump sums, by outcome.
@ref ss 14, 34K; First Schedule paras 1-3; Fifth Schedule Part 3 paras 1-3
GIVEN ame      IS A NUMBER
      born     IS A DATE
      accident IS A DATE
      o        IS AN Outcome
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lump sum for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident `, outcome` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `death` THEN `the death compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident
    WHEN `permanent or current total incapacity` THEN `the total incapacity compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident
    WHEN `permanent or current partial incapacity` p THEN `the partial incapacity compensation for an AME of` ame `, born` born `, accident on` accident `, losses in percent` (LIST p)
    WHEN `temporary incapacity` THEN REFUSE "temporary incapacity is paid periodically (s 17, 34N), not as a lump sum: use the temporary incapacity rules"

§§ `Temporary incapacity (s 17, s 34N; First Schedule para 4; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 4)`

-- First Schedule para 4(1): for each day within one year starting on the date
-- of the accident on hospitalisation leave, medical leave or light duties:
-- "(a) for the first 60 days of hospitalisation leave — the employee's AME;
-- (b) ... subsequent days ... — two-thirds ...; (c) for the first 14 days of
-- medical leave and light duties — (i) [on] medical leave — the employee's
-- AME; and (ii) [on] light duties — the shortfall (if any) in the employee's
-- actual wages for that period below the employee's AME; (d) for any
-- subsequent days ... — two-thirds of the employee's AME, [or] the shortfall
-- ... below two-thirds of the employee's AME."
-- Fifth Schedule para 4(1): the same with ADE, without light duties; para
-- 4(2): where ADE is unavailable, "$27 x D".
--
-- FORK F4: the Schedule pays "based on" AME, a MONTHLY figure, for each DAY,
-- and does not say how to turn one into the other. The daily rate is an input
-- (`daily AME`). For a platform worker the ADE is already daily.
-- FORK F5: "the first 14 days of medical leave and light duties" is one count,
-- shared by the two kinds of day, in the order the days fall.
@ref First Schedule para 4(1); Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 4(1)-(2)
GIVEN accident   IS A DATE
      `daily AME` IS A NUMBER
      days       IS A LIST OF `Leave day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the temporary incapacity payments for an accident on` accident `at a daily rate of` `daily AME` `for the days` days MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for an accident on` accident
    THEN `pay` (filter `within a year` days) 0 0
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this accident date"
    WHERE
        `within a year` ld MEANS
                ld's `day` AT LEAST accident
            AND ld's `day` LESS THAN `add years` accident 1
            AND NOT ld's `kind` EQUALS `a day that does not count`
        `two thirds` MEANS 2 DIVIDED BY 3
        `pay` ds hosp ml MEANS
            CONSIDER ds
            WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
            WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                CONSIDER d's `kind`
                WHEN `a day of hospitalisation leave` THEN
                        (IF hosp LESS THAN 60 THEN `daily AME` ELSE `daily AME` TIMES `two thirds`)
                    PLUS `pay` rest (hosp PLUS 1) ml
                WHEN `a day of medical leave` THEN
                        (IF ml LESS THAN 14 THEN `daily AME` ELSE `daily AME` TIMES `two thirds`)
                    PLUS `pay` rest hosp (ml PLUS 1)
                WHEN `a day of light duties` THEN
                        `shortfall` (IF ml LESS THAN 14 THEN `daily AME` ELSE `daily AME` TIMES `two thirds`) (d's `actual wages that day`)
                    PLUS `pay` rest hosp (ml PLUS 1)
                WHEN `a day that does not count` THEN `pay` rest hosp ml
        `shortfall` level wages MEANS IF wages LESS THAN level THEN level MINUS wages ELSE 0

-- Fifth Schedule para 4(2): "Where the platform worker's ADE is unavailable
-- ... periodical payments computed in accordance with the formula $27 x D,
-- where D is the number of days the platform worker is on hospitalisation
-- leave or medical leave."
@ref Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 4(1)-(2)
GIVEN accident IS A DATE
      e        IS A `Platform earnings`
      days     IS A LIST OF `Leave day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform worker's temporary incapacity payments for an accident on` accident `with earnings` e `for the days` days MEANS
    IF   e's `ADE available`
    THEN `the temporary incapacity payments for an accident on` accident `at a daily rate of` (`the platform worker's ADE from` e) `for the days` `leave days`
    ELSE 27 TIMES count `leave days`
    WHERE
        -- light duties are not a head for platform workers (para 4(1))
        `leave days` MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD     d's `day` AT LEAST accident
                                              AND d's `day` LESS THAN `add years` accident 1
                                              AND (   d's `kind` EQUALS `a day of hospitalisation leave`
                                                   OR d's `kind` EQUALS `a day of medical leave`)) days

-- s 17(4), s 34N(5): periodical payments "may be commuted into a lump sum, of
-- an amount agreed ..., after — (a) the periodical payments have continued for
-- not less than 6 months; and (b) the Commissioner consents."
@ref s 17(4), s 34N(5)
GIVEN `payments began on`       IS A DATE
      d                         IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the periodical payments that began on` `payments began on` `may be commuted on` d `, the Commissioner consenting:` `the Commissioner consents` IF
        d AT LEAST `add months` `payments began on` 6
    AND `the Commissioner consents`

-- s 34N(2): a platform worker's periodical payment is payable "(a) where the
-- platform operator receives, no later than the 14th day of a calendar month
-- ..., a certificate of a health professional ... — not later than 16 days
-- after the relevant day; or (b) [if received later in the month] — not later
-- than the 13th day of the following calendar month."
@ref s 34N(2)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay a platform worker's periodical payment, certificate received on` received MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY received AT MOST 14
    THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR received) (DATE_MONTH received) 14 PLUS 16
    ELSE `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR received) (DATE_MONTH received) 13) 1

-- s 17(1)(b) (employees): "payable not later than the same day as earnings
-- would have been payable ... except that the interval between periodical
-- payments must not exceed one month." The pay day is the contract's: an
-- input.
@ref s 17(1)(b)
GIVEN `previous payment on` IS A DATE
      `next payment on`     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interval from` `previous payment on` `to` `next payment on` `is within s 17(1)(b)` IF
    `next payment on` AT MOST `add months` `previous payment on` 1

§§ `Medical treatment (s 16, s 34M; First Schedule para 5; Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 5)`

-- para 5(1): "the lower of ... (a) the cost of medical treatment received ...
-- within a period of one year after the date of the accident ...; (b) ...
-- per accident per employee: (i) if the accident takes place before
-- 1 November 2025 — $45,000; (ii) ... on or after 1 November 2025 — $53,000."
-- The Fifth Schedule says "per employee" too; read as per platform worker.
@ref First Schedule para 5(1); Fifth Schedule Part 3 para 5(1)
GIVEN accident IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medical cap for an accident on` accident MEANS
    IF accident LESS THAN YMD 2025 11 1 THEN 45000 ELSE 53000

@ref ss 16(1), 34M(1); First Schedule para 5
GIVEN accident IS A DATE
      cost     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medical compensation for an accident on` accident `, the cost within a year being` cost MEANS
    IF   NOT `the law is encoded for an accident on` accident
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for this accident date"
    ELSE IF cost LESS THAN `the medical cap for an accident on` accident THEN cost ELSE `the medical cap for an accident on` accident

-- s 16(1)(a), s 34M(1): treatment "by a health professional or at an approved
-- medical institution; and ... certified by any attending health professional
-- to be necessary". s 16(1)(b): for an employee within s 9, treatment abroad
-- "required immediately due to the nature of the work injury" in the
-- Commissioner's opinion.
@ref s 16(1), s 34M(1)
GIVEN `by a health professional or at an approved institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified necessary`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `abroad, for an accident abroad, and required immediately in the Commissioner's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment is compensable:` `by a health professional or at an approved institution` `,` `certified necessary` `,` `abroad, for an accident abroad, and required immediately in the Commissioner's opinion` IF
        "(a)" ... (`by a health professional or at an approved institution` AND `certified necessary`)
    OR  "(b)" ... `abroad, for an accident abroad, and required immediately in the Commissioner's opinion`

-- s 16(2)-(3), s 34M(2)-(3): compensation for treatment at an approved medical
-- institution goes to its proprietor, "after deducting any amount previously
-- paid by or on behalf of the [worker]"; s 16(4), s 34M(4): whoever paid
-- recovers it.
@ref s 16(2), s 34M(2)
GIVEN compensation          IS A NUMBER
      `already paid to it`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid to the approved medical institution, of` compensation `, less` `already paid to it` MEANS
    IF compensation GREATER THAN `already paid to it` THEN compensation MINUS `already paid to it` ELSE 0

§§ `Seafarers (s 67)`

-- s 67(1): no periodical payment for temporary incapacity while the ship's
-- owner is liable to defray the seafarer's maintenance under a shipping law
-- (other than the Maritime Labour Convention Act). s 67(2): medical
-- compensation is reduced by any payment under s 35 of the Merchant Shipping
-- (Maritime Labour Convention) Act 2014. s 67(3): temporary incapacity
-- compensation is reduced by any payment under its s 36.
@ref s 67(2), (3)
GIVEN compensation IS A NUMBER
      received     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the seafarer's compensation of` compensation `, reduced by` received MEANS
    IF compensation GREATER THAN received THEN compensation MINUS received ELSE 0

@ref s 67(1)
GIVEN `the owner is liable for maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a periodical payment is payable to the seafarer, the owner liable for maintenance:` `the owner is liable for maintenance` IF
    NOT `the owner is liable for maintenance`

§§ `Refusal of treatment (s 38)`

-- s 38: where the worker "refuses treatment ... or fails to carry out or
-- deliberately disregards the instructions of a health professional", the
-- Commissioner MAY suspend or restrict periodical payments, or pay permanent
-- or current incapacity compensation for the incapacity that would have
-- resulted with the treatment. A discretion; its trigger is encoded.
@ref s 38
GIVEN `refused, failed or disregarded treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may direct under s 38, treatment having been refused:` `refused, failed or disregarded treatment` IF
    `refused, failed or disregarded treatment`
